WEBVTT

00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:17.220
This is the one that's all over the news. AI agents: models that browse the web, write code, book flights. It sounds like a whole new kind of technology. It isn't. It's the loop you've already run, with one rule added.

00:00:18.610 --> 00:00:29.100
Here's the rule. Fill the cup and draw, exactly as before. But the moment you draw a punctuation mark, a full stop, a comma, stop. That's a tool call.

00:00:30.150 --> 00:00:40.980
So the model doesn't decide to use a tool. It draws one, like any other word. Some rows almost never call it. Some always do.

00:00:42.230 --> 00:00:53.980
Say you've written "here comes the dog". The row for "dog": two red for a full stop, two blue for "runs". Draw one. Red. Full stop. Stop.

00:00:54.590 --> 00:01:02.680
The tool is a text message. Send "What comes next?", and the sentence so far, to three friends or group chats.

00:01:03.910 --> 00:01:12.340
The first reply back is your tool result. Write the whole thing down, then the full stop you drew. Then carry on, from the full stop.

00:01:13.030 --> 00:01:22.860
Why from the full stop, and not from "sandwich"? Because nobody has a row for "sandwich". But there's always a row for a full stop.

00:01:24.350 --> 00:01:30.480
Replies take time. If nothing's back by your next punctuation mark, leave a gap and fill it in later.

00:01:31.310 --> 00:01:48.280
Here's the bit that matters. The model never learned what comes next after "the dog". It only drew when to ask. And the thing that paused it, sent the message, and spliced the answer back in? That was you. You were the harness.

00:01:49.690 --> 00:01:59.440
Take the person out, and you've got a model acting on its own. That's what the news means by an agent. So: what would you let it do without asking you first?

00:02:00.310 --> 00:02:05.100
Don't answer yet. In a few minutes, your group will be the harness.
